{"k":"h","w":0,"an":["_jwpo0th8sz0r"],"l":1,"title":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"A VOCABULARY AND CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK DESCRIBING AND CATEGORISING EMOTIONS","b":1,"u":1}]},
{"k":"gap","w":9},
{"k":"h","w":9,"an":["_yxch549xhuvi"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"1. Basic Emotions","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":12,"r":[{"t":"Basic emotions are often considered universal and biologically hardwired. According to Paul Ekman, there are six primary emotions:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":30},
{"k":"li","w":31,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"3","r":[{"t":"Happiness","b":1},{"t":": Joy, pleasure, contentment"}]},
{"k":"li","w":36,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"3","r":[{"t":"Sadness","b":1},{"t":": Grief, sorrow, unhappiness"}]},
{"k":"li","w":41,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"c)","n":"3","r":[{"t":"Fear","b":1},{"t":": Anxiety, apprehension, terror"}]},
{"k":"li","w":46,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"d)","n":"3","r":[{"t":"Anger","b":1},{"t":": Rage, frustration, irritation"}]},
{"k":"li","w":51,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"e)","n":"3","r":[{"t":"Surprise","b":1},{"t":": Astonishment, shock, amazement"}]},
{"k":"li","w":56,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"f)","n":"3","r":[{"t":"Disgust","b":1},{"t":": Revulsion, contempt, disdain"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":60},
{"k":"h","w":60,"an":["_isjoh6ovzouv"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"2. Complex Emotions","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":63,"r":[{"t":"Complex emotions are combinations of basic emotions and are influenced by cultural and social factors. Examples include:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":80},
{"k":"li","w":81,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"9","r":[{"t":"Love","b":1},{"t":": Combination of joy and trust (intimacy and passion)"}]},
{"k":"li","w":91,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"9","r":[{"t":"Jealousy","b":1},{"t":": Combination of anger, fear, and sadness"}]},
{"k":"li","w":99,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"c)","n":"9","r":[{"t":"Guilt","b":1},{"t":": Combination of sadness and fear"}]},
{"k":"li","w":106,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"d)","n":"9","r":[{"t":"Pride","b":1},{"t":": Combination of joy and satisfaction"}]},
{"k":"li","w":113,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"e)","n":"9","r":[{"t":"Shame","b":1},{"t":": Combination of sadness and fear (often with a social or moral component)"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":126},
{"k":"h","w":126,"an":["_cbib6kh3gwh1"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"3. Emotional Dimensions","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":129,"r":[{"t":"Emotions can be categorized along different dimensions:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":136},
{"k":"li","w":137,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"1","r":[{"t":"Valence","b":1},{"t":": Positive (e.g., happiness) vs. Negative (e.g., sadness)"}]},
{"k":"li","w":146,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"1","r":[{"t":"Arousal","b":1},{"t":": High arousal (e.g., anger) vs. Low arousal (e.g., calmness)"}]},
{"k":"li","w":157,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"c)","n":"1","r":[{"t":"Intensity","b":1},{"t":": Mild (e.g., annoyance) vs. Intense (e.g., rage)"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":165},
{"k":"h","w":165,"an":["_llla1evpvnxo"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"4. Emotional Domains","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":168,"r":[{"t":"Emotions can be grouped based on contexts and experiences:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":177},
{"k":"li","w":178,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"6","r":[{"t":"Self-conscious emotions","b":1},{"t":": Guilt, shame, pride, embarrassment"}]},
{"k":"li","w":185,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"6","r":[{"t":"Social emotions","b":1},{"t":": Empathy, jealousy, envy, gratitude"}]},
{"k":"li","w":192,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"c)","n":"6","r":[{"t":"Moral emotions","b":1},{"t":": Guilt, shame, pride, empathy"}]},
{"k":"li","w":199,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"d)","n":"6","r":[{"t":"Achievement emotions","b":1},{"t":": Pride, satisfaction, frustration, disappointment"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":205},
{"k":"h","w":205,"an":["_8fbjcw9l8mb5"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"5. The Circumplex Model of Affect","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":211,"r":[{"t":"This model, proposed by James Russell, positions emotions on a circular arrangement along two dimensions: valence (pleasure-displeasure) and arousal (activation-deactivation)."}]},
{"k":"gap","w":231},
{"k":"li","w":232,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"10","r":[{"t":"High Arousal & Positive Valence","b":1},{"t":": Excitement, enthusiasm"}]},
{"k":"li","w":240,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"10","r":[{"t":"High Arousal & Negative Valence","b":1},{"t":": Anger, anxiety"}]},
{"k":"li","w":248,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"c)","n":"10","r":[{"t":"Low Arousal & Positive Valence","b":1},{"t":": Contentment, relaxation"}]},
{"k":"li","w":256,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"d)","n":"10","r":[{"t":"Low Arousal & Negative Valence","b":1},{"t":": Sadness, depression"}]},
{"k":"img","w":263,"i":"i1","wh":[583,528]},
{"k":"gap","w":263},
{"k":"h","w":263,"an":["_rdjv4xp2x8tl"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"6. The Plutchik's Wheel of Emotions","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":269,"r":[{"t":"Robert Plutchik's model identifies eight primary emotions, each with varying degrees of intensity, and proposes their combinations to form more complex emotions."}]},
{"k":"gap","w":291},
{"k":"li","w":292,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"4","r":[{"t":"Primary Emotions","b":1},{"t":": Joy, trust, fear, surprise, sadness, disgust, anger, anticipation"}]},
{"k":"li","w":303,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"4","r":[{"t":"Secondary Emotions","b":1},{"t":": Formed by combinations of primary emotions (e.g., joy + trust = love)"}]},
{"k":"img","w":317,"i":"i2","wh":[463,692]},
{"k":"gap","w":317},
{"k":"h","w":317,"an":["_nb2xfsuit7aa"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"7. Emotional Regulation","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":320,"r":[{"t":"The processes by which individuals influence their emotions, including:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":329},
{"k":"li","w":330,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"2","r":[{"t":"Cognitive Reappraisal","b":1},{"t":": Changing the way one thinks about a situation"}]},
{"k":"li","w":341,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"2","r":[{"t":"Expressive Suppression","b":1},{"t":": Inhibiting the outward signs of emotions"}]},
{"k":"li","w":350,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"c)","n":"2","r":[{"t":"Mindfulness","b":1},{"t":": Awareness and acceptance of one's current emotions"}]},
{"k":"li","w":359,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"d)","n":"2","r":[{"t":"Problem-solving","b":1},{"t":": Addressing the source of the emotion"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":366},
{"k":"h","w":366,"an":["_mqp8g7ngs2h0"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"8. Emotional Intelligence","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":369,"r":[{"t":"[1]","sup":1},{"t":"The ability to identify, understand, manage, and utilize emotions effectively:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":379},
{"k":"li","w":380,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"7","r":[{"t":"Self-awareness: Recognizing one's own emotions"}]},
{"k":"li","w":386,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"7","r":[{"t":"Self-regulation: Managing one's own emotions"}]},
{"k":"li","w":392,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"c)","n":"7","r":[{"t":"Social awareness: Recognizing emotions in others"}]},
{"k":"li","w":399,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"d)","n":"7","r":[{"t":"Relationship management: Handling interpersonal relationships judiciously and empathetically"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":407},
{"k":"h","w":407,"an":["_ftv1ve57nysn"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"9. Cultural Influences on Emotions","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":412,"r":[{"t":"Different cultures express and interpret emotions uniquely, affecting emotional experience and expression:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":424},
{"k":"li","w":425,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"5","r":[{"t":"Display rules","b":1},{"t":": Cultural norms about how and when emotions should be expressed"}]},
{"k":"li","w":438,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"5","r":[{"t":"Emotion lexicon","b":1},{"t":": The vocabulary a language has for emotions, which can influence emotional awareness and expression"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":454},
{"k":"h","w":454,"an":["_jgeswwx8bd9p"],"l":1,"al":"c","r":[{"t":"10. Physiological Basis of Emotions","b":1}]},
{"k":"p","w":459,"r":[{"t":"Emotions are linked to physiological responses in the body, involving:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":469},
{"k":"li","w":470,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"a)","n":"8","r":[{"t":"The brain","b":1},{"t":": Amygdala, prefrontal cortex, and other areas involved in emotion processing"}]},
{"k":"li","w":483,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"b)","n":"8","r":[{"t":"Autonomic nervous system","b":1},{"t":": Sympathetic and parasympathetic responses (e.g., heart rate, sweating)"}]},
{"k":"li","w":495,"list":"ol","l":0,"m":"c)","n":"8","r":[{"t":"Hormones","b":1},{"t":": Adrenaline, cortisol, and others affecting emotional states"}]},
